- **P1 — SPEC ownership can disappear on install rerun.** Continuity is asserted from the prior manifest at [scripts/install.sh:2334](/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/repass-r2.aWHxOR/wt/scripts/install.sh:2334), but the replacement manifest enumerates only files currently present at [scripts/_framework_manifest_set.sh:345](/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/repass-r2.aWHxOR/wt/scripts/_framework_manifest_set.sh:345). An empty—or zero-source-intersection—managed `SPEC/v1` therefore emits no SPEC records. Subsequent upgrades misclassify it as an adopter fork and never restore the compliance contract. The committed expected-red ledger itself labels this an open product defect.

- **P1 — LINK confinement still over-claims adopter symlinks.** `_wbm_link_allowed` permits every symlink whenever `FMS_LINK_PATHS` is unset at [scripts/_framework_manifest_set.sh:275](/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/repass-r2.aWHxOR/wt/scripts/_framework_manifest_set.sh:275), while install exports link mode without deriving prior LINK paths at [scripts/install.sh:2277](/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/repass-r2.aWHxOR/wt/scripts/install.sh:2277). A link-mode install/rerun over an existing adopter tree can consequently serialize an adopter-owned symlink inside `.claude/hooks/` or another enumerated directory as framework-owned. The upgrade symlink-probe fallback has the same unset-list behavior at [scripts/upgrade.sh:3183](/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/repass-r2.aWHxOR/wt/scripts/upgrade.sh:3183).

- **P2 — Legitimately stale protocol pointers are treated as adopter edits.** The live pointer is compared with the newly rendered canonical digest at [scripts/upgrade.sh:1625](/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/repass-r2.aWHxOR/wt/scripts/upgrade.sh:1625), not with its prior manifest digest. Changing `--profile`, `--stack`, or the pointer template makes a previously pristine pointer classify as `edited`, so it is preserved indefinitely instead of refreshed.

- **P2 — External-target pre-v1.3 `--pin` downgrades report the wrong version.** The marker record is dropped and readers are told to fall back to `VERSION` at [scripts/upgrade.sh:2134](/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/repass-r2.aWHxOR/wt/scripts/upgrade.sh:2134), although external-target upgrades deliberately never update that root file. The fallback can therefore advertise rc.2 while the installed content is pinned to an older release.

Justification: Bash syntax, ShellCheck, diff hygiene, AGENTS freshness, and count checks passed, and the described mechanical model-ledger bump adds no separate blocker. Nevertheless, the two P1 paths violate the central delivery-record invariant by either losing framework ownership or claiming adopter content, so this payload is unsafe for the cut.

